  "description": "The interface names of the commons: Yantra4D's cdg_interfaces geometry types, Fashion Cabinet's hyperobject.interfaces types, and the per-cartridge interface ids that recur often enough to be vocabulary. Both type sets are closed enums in their own schema, so the drift this document exists for is not inside a repo but ACROSS the two — the B2 problem, `zipper_tape` against `tape_edge` — plus the two within-repo dialect splits the capture turned up (sew_face/sew_plate, strap_slot/webbing_slot). The 805 y4d and 577 FC interface ids are not enumerated here: an id is a cartridge's own name for its own feature, and only the ones that recur across cartridges, or that carry a cross-commons equivalence, are vocabulary. The sheet commons (pliego, sheet-hyperobjects) joined on 2026-10-10: its eleven hyperobject.interfaces types are recorded with their counts, and the pivot carries the one cross-commons equivalence the evidence supports (a post through holes in stacked layers, the solid rivet).",
